The changes cpd made on top (docs/implementing.md, "The compact-tools extension", point 1):
- Defaults (compact-tools-config.ts DEFAULT_CONFIG): fold "toggle", toggle { expand U+F0B26, collapse U+F0B2C }, tools read, write, edit, bash, grep, find, ls. The schema's defaults follow, and the description of "toggle" says so.
- No release notice: compact-tools-release.ts is not copied; its import and its two uses in compact-tools.ts go, and the onVisible callback of SilentModeController with them.
- Erasable syntax only: the constructor parameter properties of compact-tools-activity.ts, -codex-rows.ts, -grouping.ts, -layout.ts, -progress.ts, -runtime.ts and -silent.ts (the last one's onVisible parameter is the previous item) are explicit fields assigned in the constructor.
- The policy-neutral guard: the five comments that cited a record id (compact-tools.ts, -config.ts, -layout.ts, -thinking.ts, -types.ts) cite docs/contract.md section 6.9 instead. The rule: no record id (`pro-...` or `hs-...`) in any `.ts` file under `pi/compact-tools/` or `pi/lib/`; such a comment cites `docs/contract.md section 6.9` instead.
- The double load: the new module compact-tools-double-load.ts and the early return of the factory in compact-tools.ts.
- The compaction fold: the new module compact-tools-compaction.ts re-draws pi's compaction notice as contract section 6.9 'The compaction fold'.
- The compaction cue: compact-tools-progress.ts listens to session_before_compact, session_compact and session_compact_failed; compact-tools-editor.ts paints a compaction indicator as the running pill; and compact-tools-compaction.ts mounts the running fold widget while compaction runs; each as docs/contract.md section 6.9 specifies.
- One comment of compact-tools-codex-rows.ts quoted a corner glyph after the word "from", which the import scan of pi/test/compact-tools/layout.test.ts reads as an import; it names the glyph instead.
